90","id":6133569336,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSvmECc8AAAABbZbXOA","user":{"login":"shipyard-local[bot]","id":288178668,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOES1B7A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25807?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/shipyard-local","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shipyard-local%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T22:12:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T22:12:59Z","body":"## Independent review: tartci#490 at head 82eeaab8a6bd69b02cbc83d03fb31886e2b81ad9\n\nThe latest READY comment names this head (`READY head:82eeaab8…`), and it is still the PR head. The PR is BEHIND main. It merges cleanly with main, #483 and #489 (0 conflicts in every pairing).\n\n### CI on this head: RED\n- `lint`: **failure** (https://github.com/danielraffel/tartci/actions/runs/38308502131/job/115008243160). Two tests fail: `test_install_macos_fleet…test_failed_final_verification_restores_prior_wrapper_generation` (1 != 0) and `…test_failed_receipt_publication_restores_dangling_target_symlink` (0 != 1).\n- `python-39-tests`: success.\n- `python-floor`: success.\n- Control: main at `64fa40c` and at the merge base `a52f20f` are green on `lint`.\n\n### Must-fix\n1. **The red `lint` is caused by this PR's installer reorder.** It is not pre-existing, and it is not specific to Python 3.9.\n   - **Mechanism:** both failing tests inject a fault by putting a fake `python3` first on `PATH`.\n     - The old installer resolved `python3` first, so it used the fake.\n     - The new installer sources `toml-python.lib.sh`, which tries `python3.12` and then `python3.11` **before** `python3`.\n     - On `ubuntu-latest` a `python3.12` is on PATH. The fake is bypassed, the injected failure never happens, and both assertions flip.\n   - **Reproduced locally with a control:**\n     - Plain PATH on this head: both tests pass. This host has no `python3.12`, which is why the READY saw them green.\n     - `PATH=/tmp/py312bin:$PATH`, with `python3.12` symlinked to python3.14: **both fail** at this head.\n     - Same PATH with main's `install_macos_fleet.sh` restored: both pass.\n   - **Fix:** make the fixtures inject the fault through the interpreter the installer will actually select. Either pass `TARTCI_PYTHON=<fake>` (the fake must `import tomllib` successfully, which it does via `exec sys.executable`), or shadow `python3.12`/`python3.11` as well.\n\n### Behaviour review\n- **Builder order.** Aligning the installer to the builder's order (`python3.12`, `python3.11`, `python3`, then absolute Homebrew/usr-local paths) is right: a manual install now pins the same interpreter a sealed launcher renders. In the self-update path, the orchestrator always sets `TARTCI_PYTHON` explicitly (`fleet_self_update.py:1176`), so the order does not affect self-update.\n- **m1's `/usr/bin` shims.** `/usr/bin/python3` (3.9) fails the `import tomllib` probe in both old and new code, so neither will pin it. Under launchd's minimal PATH, resolution falls through to the absolute Homebrew candidates, as before.\n- **Stricter `TARTCI_PYTHON`.** `TARTCI_PYTHON` naming a non-tomllib interpreter is now refused early with exit 127 instead of later. That fails closed and says so.\n\n### Tests that cannot fail\nI restored main's `build_macos_launcher.sh` on this head. All 15 `test_signing_prompt_guard` tests still pass.\n- `test_launcher_builder_reports_missing_interpreter` passes against main's builder, because the old builder already exits non-zero with stderr through `canonical_python`. It does not cover the new explicit message.\n- The two `LauncherBuildTests` are useful regression coverage of the real render, but they do not pin this PR's change either.\n- No test covers the installer reorder. `test_install_macos_fleet.py` is unchanged, so main's installer passes the same suite.\n\n### Should-fix\n- Assert the new message text (`requires a Python 3.11+ interpreter`) in the missing-interpreter test so that it fails against main.\n- Add an installer test showing that, with `python3.12` and `python3` both on PATH and no `TARTCI_PYTHON`, the installer pins the same interpreter as `build_macos_launcher.sh --print-render-python`.\n- The new symlink walk over `$TARTCI_PYTHON` in `install_macos_fleet.sh` computes `python_probe` but uses it only for cycle refusal. Either use it or say in a comment that cycle refusal is its only purpose.\n- On a host with a per-binary egress firewall, preferring `python3.12` over `python3` can pick an interpreter the firewall has not approved. The `probe_interpreter_github.py` gate catches that loudly (exit 127), so it is not silent. Worth a line in the runbook.\n\n### Local runs (python3.14, macOS)\n- `test_signing_prompt_guard`: 15/15 OK.\n- `test_install_macos_fleet`: 55 tests, 54 pass and 1 fails. The failure is `test_installed_agent_hygiene_wrapper_keeps_human_only_gate`, which depends on the host (\"sessions older than 2d\") and was already noted in the earlier review of #489.\n\nverdict: HOLD head:82eeaab8a6bd69b02cbc83d03fb31886e2b81ad9\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/danielraffel/tartci/issues/comments/6133569336/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":3878000,"client_id":"Iv23liTCzDQWqmMjkDTI","slug":"shipyard-local","node_id":"A_kwDNZM_OADsscA","owner":{"login":"danielraffel","id":25807,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1ODA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25807?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel","html_url":"https://github.com/danielraffel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielraffel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Shipyard Local","description":"","external_url":"https://github.com/danielraffel/shipyard","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/shipyard-local","created_at":"2026-05-27T01:32:23Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T08:42:04Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","actions_variables":"write","administration":"write","agent_secrets":"write","agent_tasks":"write","agent_variables":"write","artifact_metadata":"write","attestations":"write","checks":"write","codespaces":"write","codespaces_lifecycle_admin":"write","codespaces_metadata":"read","codespaces_secrets":"write","code_quality":"write","contents":"write","copilot_agent_settings":"write","dependabot_secrets":"write","deployments":"write","discussions":"write","environments":"write","issues":"write","license_compliance_alerts":"write","merge_queues"